$conn = mysqli_connect("localhost", "school_user", "secret", "school_db");
if (!$conn) { die("Connection failed: " . mysqli_connect_error()); }
mysqli_set_charset($conn, "utf8mb4");
Connection = link between program and DBMS (server, user, password, database); all SQL is sent through it; closed at the end. Kept in connect.php and included with require.

INSERT adds new records: INSERT INTO table (field1, field2) VALUES (value1, value2); values in the same order as the fields.
All fields: INSERT INTO Student VALUES (6, 'Nursultan', 11, 'Astana', '2009-09-01');
Named fields (recommended): INSERT INTO Student (Name, Grade, City) VALUES ('Nursultan', 11, 'Astana');
Several: INSERT INTO Student (Name, Grade) VALUES ('Ali', 10), ('Dana', 12);
Number of fields must equal number of values.

$sql = "INSERT INTO Student (Name, Grade, City) VALUES ('$name', $grade, '$city')";
if (mysqli_query($conn, $sql)) echo "Added, ID " . mysqli_insert_id($conn); else echo "Error: " . mysqli_error($conn);
mysqli_query → true/false; mysqli_insert_id → new auto-increment ID (e.g. order number, foreign key for order lines); mysqli_affected_rows → number of records added/changed.

UPDATE Student SET City = 'Almaty' WHERE StudentID = 4;
DELETE FROM Student WHERE StudentID = 4;
Without WHERE every record in the table is changed / deleted.

Prepared statement = SQL sent with placeholders ? and compiled first; values bound and sent separately, so input is always data, never code.
$stmt = mysqli_prepare($conn, "INSERT INTO Student (Name, Grade, City) VALUES (?, ?, ?)");
mysqli_stmt_bind_param($stmt, "sis", $name, $grade, $city);
mysqli_stmt_execute($stmt);
s = string (also dates), i = integer, d = double, b = blob. Validation does NOT stop injection — placeholders do. Output: htmlspecialchars() against XSS.
